    "title": "LEAD L-01: Untrusted-prize requirement exceeds the interface's honest-ERC721 assumption",
    "description": "The clean requirements call arbitrary prize contracts untrusted, while IRaffle states that supported prizes are honest standards-compliant ERC721s. The factory checks self-reported ERC165 support, the receiver transition, and ownerOf after escrow; those checks cannot establish future transfer behavior. In a reserve-met result, settlement can allocate the full pot to sponsor and treasury independently of NFT delivery. If an admitted prize subsequently refuses transfer, redemption reverts atomically but NftWon has no refund transition. This is a concrete conditional liveness/trust-boundary path, not a demonstrated exploit or a finding against an honest compliant prize: no particular hostile prize implementation is present in the pinned context. Keep as a lead until the intended prize trust boundary and an applicable concrete prize behavior are established. Defensive obligation: state the supported prize trust assumptions explicitly and assess whether the intended winner exit must survive permanent prize-delivery failure.\nAssumptions: DESIGN.md is authoritative for the requirement that arbitrary prize contracts are untrusted; interface comments are evidence of a narrower implementation assumption, not permission to narrow the audit.; The conditional delivery failure requires prize behavior not instantiated by a prize implementation in this context. No claim of an executed or confirmed loss path is made.; Canonical USDC and the configured Chainlink wrapper behave according to the stated trusted dependency model.",
